+### Compound Format
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })                // "1h30m"
+ms(25 * 3600000 + 30 * 60000, { compound: true }) // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })               // "-1h30m"
+```
+
+Units are combined largest first with no separators, zero parts are skipped, hours are the largest unit and seconds the smallest (leftover milliseconds are dropped). The output is compatible with Go's `time.ParseDuration`. `compound` is ignored when `long` is set.
+
